ewline (queue 293): the tokenizer asks for the line's rest at ps2 and meets the"] [112 5 "// end of input, its newline written (tok_underflow_interactive, PyOS_StdioReadline), before the statement runs"] [131 4 "// run_mod's interactive source (queue 223): the statement's lines registered with linecache, so traceback's"] [132 4 "// display shows them as the Go display did from RegisterSource"] [135 29 "// __main__'s namespace after the main module under -i (queue 289)"] [154 1 "// replSyntaxText gives a compiler's SyntaxError of the interactive source src (a symbol table's: \"duplicate argument\")"] [155 1 "// its line, which the file \"<stdin>\" cannot give (syntaxError's kind c reads the file): CPython's REPL compiles the"] [156 1 "// statement under a name linecache holds its source by (run_mod's interactive source, \"<stdin-N>\"), so the report shows"] [157 1 "// the line and its caret (test_repl's test_runsource_show_syntax_error_location; queue 293)."] [185 1 "// runPyrepl is _pymain_run_repl's terminal branch (Modules/main.c of CPython 3.14.10; queue 298): on a terminal, unless"] [186 1 "// PYTHON_BASIC_REPL is set (not under -E or -I), _pyrepl imported and _pyrepl.main.interactive_console(mainmodule="] [187 1 "// __main__, pythonstartup=startup) run as pymain_run_pyrepl calls it; the status and true, or false when _pyrepl is not"] [188 1 "// found (the basic REPL then). An error is printed as pymain_exit_err_print prints it (SystemExit: its status)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[52 53] [55 30] [134 55] [142 29] [163 29] [200 28] [210 41] [211 28] [216 46]]} (go/file "repl.go" :imports [


